    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0420" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/570a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-14T23:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>112. Please deliver a paraphrase of following secret message signed
                        Marshall<anchor n="54" xml:id="d501-f1"/> to Amler<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d501-f2"/> at Harbel.</p>
                <pb facs="0421" n="409" xml:id="pg409"/>
                <p>If the British request further use of facilities which have been granted us in
                    Liberia, they should be informed that the British staff in Washington is the
                    channel through which such a request should be made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d501-f1" n="54" xml:id="d501-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. George C. Marshall, Chief of Staff, U. S. Army.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d501-f2" n="55" xml:id="d501-f2-content">
                <p>Code name for Commanding Officer, United States Forces in Liberia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
